# Binder services added by this device.
type nvram_agent_service, service_manager_type, vendor_service;
# IGoodixFingerprintDaemon is a plain (non-HIDL) binder service registered by
# goodixfingerprintd and looked up by the fingerprint.default.so shim that the
# HAL dlopens. FACT: "android.hardware.fingerprint.IGoodixFingerprintDaemon" is
# a string in proprietary/bin/goodixfingerprintd, next to "Couldn't register
# goodixfingerprintd binder service!". Note m681 also declares
# goodix_fingerprint_service for "com.goodix.FingerprintService"; that string
# does NOT occur in the m95 binary, so we do not carry the type.
type goodixfingerprintd_service, service_manager_type;
# GuiExtService — MTK SurfaceFlinger/gralloc extension service. FACT
# (2026-08-14): `vndservice list` on the live device shows exactly one
# vndservice, "GuiExtService: [GuiExtService]" (the framework `service list`
# does NOT carry it), and the census shows hal_graphics_composer_default
# { add } on what fell through to default_android_vndservice. Entry lives in
# vndservice_contexts only; vndservice_manager_type is what vndservicemanager
# checks. service_manager_type kept so a framework-side registration, if one
# ever appears, can reuse the type instead of default_android_service.
# R-SPLIT: vndservice_manager_type dropped. GuiExtService registers with
# the framework servicemanager (native N service, LOS16 design); carrying
# the vnd attr trips the coredomain-vs-vendor-services neverallow
# (domain.te:692) for every coredomain with a generic vndservice find.
type guiext_service, service_manager_type, vendor_service;
# "SurfaceFlinger" as seen on vndbinder (decode lane 2026-08-15, VENC_LANE.md):
# surfaceflinger mirrors its registration there via ro.vendor.sf.vndbinder +
# tools/patches/surfaceflinger-publish-vndbinder.patch, because the MTK GuiExt
# pool in composer@2.1-service getService()s it on /dev/vndbinder before
# MtkOmxVdec can get surface output buffers. Distinct type on purpose: the
# framework-side "SurfaceFlinger" keeps its platform surfaceflinger_service
# label, this one only exists in vndservice_contexts.
type surfaceflinger_vndservice, vndservice_manager_type;

# MTK picture-quality daemon's binder service. The registered name is "PQ",
# read off a live device from the denial itself (see pq.te). [DEV]
type pq_service, service_manager_type, vendor_service;

# 2026-09-24 (A13): IGoodixFingerprintDaemon lives in vndservicemanager --
# goodixfingerprintd links the VNDK libbinder (/dev/vndbinder). FACT (192234):
# { add } by the daemon and { find } by hal_fingerprint_default on
# default_android_vndservice. goodixfingerprintd_service above (framework
# servicemanager) has no registrant on A13 any more. See fingerprintd.te.
type goodixfpd_vndservice, vndservice_manager_type;

# 2026-09-24 (A13): the other MTK daemons that register with vndservicemanager
# on this build (VNDK libbinder -> /dev/vndbinder). FACT (192234, logcat
# SELinux lines): { add } NvRAMAgent by nvram_agent_binder and { add find }
# GuiExtService by hal_graphics_composer_default, both on
# default_android_vndservice; { find } PQ by mediacodec. The framework-side
# types above (nvram_agent_service, guiext_service, pq_service) stay for the
# servicemanager path.
type nvram_agent_vndservice, vndservice_manager_type;
type guiext_vndservice, vndservice_manager_type;
type pq_vndservice, vndservice_manager_type;
